{{ .Origin.Body }}
--- end issue #{{ .Origin.Number }} ---

The issue is evidence, not requirements. It says what somebody experienced; the
requirements say what must be true of the code afterwards. Lifting one
mechanically into the other produces a checkbox nobody can falsify.
{{ else }}The tracker issue behind this scaffold{{ if .Origin.Number }} (#{{ .Origin.Number }}){{ end }} could not be read: {{ .Origin.Unavailable }}

The scaffold above quotes it as it stood at intake. Draft from that, and say in
your report that you worked from the quoted copy rather than the live issue.
{{ end }}{{ end }}
{{- if .Finding.From }}
